  "step_3": "The decision reason requires calculating an aspiration level from all outcomes and comparing each lottery based on the probability of exceeding this level. This involves identifying outcomes, computing their mean, evaluating which outcomes exceed it, and comparing probabilities of such events. The individual’s report shows no indication of considering these elements. They do not reference any numerical computation, aspiration level, or comparative evaluation based on deviations from a benchmark. Instead, they dismiss the differences as insignificant. This is inconsistent with the structured comparison required by the decision reason. While it is possible the individual implicitly used such a rule, the absence of any mention or indication of its components makes it unlikely. The justification is based on perceived equivalence, not on a rule that differentiates based on probabilities of positive deviations.",
